# kills: the pan does not move when the seed goes bad
# suite: node --test --test-name-pattern ^the.pan.does.not.move.when.the.seed.goes.bad$ tests/e2e.test.js
# The parse line stops leaving the flow when it is blank, so on an invalid seed
# it holds its reserved row AND #scale-refusal adds a second one below it - the
# two-line reservation the Edit sheet cannot afford. The pan steps down a line
# under the finger at 380px, exactly where the owner is looking. Every text,
# tier and aria-live assertion still passes; only the preview's top edge sees
# it. This is the rule that pays for the move, so this is the mutant.
diff --git a/index.html b/index.html
--- a/index.html
+++ b/index.html
@@ -500,7 +500,7 @@ button.nav:active{background:#2e281e}
    26.59px under the finger, and put #scale-layout-row's bottom at 785.69
    against a 780px viewport - below the fold, the exact cost this row exists
    to avoid. #scale-msg is back below the pan and never enters this row. */
-#scale-parse:empty, #scale-refusal:empty{display:none}
+#scale-refusal:empty{display:none}
 /* The pan mock sits on a light plate because the pan is drawn in card ink -
    black rim, #242424 labels - and the sheet surface is dark. Capped so the
    whole sheet still fits a 380px phone without the preview pushing GENERATE
